fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: chalk_lead
name: The Lead
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Named, durability 3, attack +2, rating 8.
  level: 3
  role: standard
  armor: 0
  morale: 7
  weapon: Grit, and a rust-brown seam
  wants: Whatever the pack has already failed to catch.
  special: UNMAKING RUN — once per scene, the Lead runs the whole length of the pack's road,
    and every chalk hound that has come apart this scene reassembles behind it.
  when_bloodied: It stops holding back. If it has not made its Unmaking Run yet, it makes
    it now.
  tells: One of the pack is a head taller than the rest, with a rust-brown seam through it,
    and it has not run yet. It is watching the pass.
  breaks: Withdraws down its own road and takes what is left of the pack with it. It does
    not follow anyone off the road; it has never been off the road.
  twists:
  - 'The seam is wet: something bled on this road last night.'
  - It holds back through the whole fight and runs only when someone tries to leave.
  - The road ends at a bridge that is out, and the Lead knows exactly where the drop is.
  - Two roads cross here, and two packs are contesting the crossing.
  - It has started running beside one carter's cart every night, and only that cart.
  - The pack is down to the Lead and two hounds, and it runs harder than any full pack.
  nastier: It can make the Unmaking Run twice a scene, and the hounds it reassembles attack
    in the exchange they come back.
  description: >-
    The oldest dust on the road, and the only one of the pack with a colour to it — a rust-brown
    seam through the chalk where something bled here a long time ago. It is a head taller
    than the others and it never runs first.
  notes: >-
    Level 3 standard: no overrides.


    Patient in a way none of its pack is. It holds back through the first exchange and joins
    on the second, and it spends the Unmaking Run the moment three or more hounds are down.


    Appears: one per pack, and a pack per road.
  reskin_of: null
